🎯 Found it. This is why your login keeps bouncing back.

The bug is here:

// Create a session
req.session.regenerate = {
    _id: user._id,
    username: user.username.toLowerCase().trim(),
    email: user.email.toLowerCase().trim(),
    role: user.role || "user"
};

console.log("Session after login:", req.session.user);
❌ What's wrong?
You assigned the user object to:

req.session.regenerate
But regenerate is not where session data belongs.

In express-session, regenerate is actually a method (function) used to create a new session ID. 
By assigning an object to it, you're overwriting that method instead of storing user data.

That's why:

console.log(req.session.user);
prints:

undefined
because you never set req.session.user.

✅ The fix
Replace this:

req.session.regenerate = {
    _id: user._id,
