Exactly. You've found the reason. 👍

Your middleware currently does this:

if (!roles.includes(req.session.user.role)) {
    return res.status(403).send("Access Denied.");
}
That sends plain text to the browser, so Express never renders your 403.ejs.

Change it to render the view
Replace it with:

exports.allowRoles = (...roles) => {

    return (req, res, next) => {

        if (!req.session.user) {
            return res.redirect("/auth/login");
        }

        if (!roles.includes(req.session.user.role)) {
            return res.status(403).render("403", {
                pageTitle: "Access Denied"
            });
        }

        next();

    };

};
Now, whenever a logged-in user doesn't have one of the required roles, they'll see your custom 403 page.

