That sequence is interesting.

If you can access homeForm, then you already passed the role middleware on the GET request.

If you then get a 403 after clicking Submit, it suggests one of these possibilities:

The GET and POST routes are protected differently.

Your session is changing between the GET and POST requests.

The POST route requires different roles.

For example:

// GET
router.get(
    "/new",
    authMiddleware.isLoggedIn,
    roleMiddleware.allowRoles(ROLES.ADMIN),
    predictionController.newPrediction
);

// POST
router.post(
    "/",
    authMiddleware.isLoggedIn,
    roleMiddleware.allowRoles(ROLES.SUPERUSER),
    predictionController.createPrediction
);
In that case, an admin could open the form but not submit it.

